        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128292743?u=3e557f09456339e289afa5d06625e4c955e0a4e6&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Add the missing <code class=\"notranslate\">idle-detection</code> permission descriptor to <code class=\"notranslate\">api/Permissions.json</code>.</li>\n<li>Reuse browser support and status metadata from the existing <code class=\"notranslate\">api/IdleDetector.json</code> entry.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Local schema validation was not run. The support data follows the existing <code class=\"notranslate\">IdleDetector</code> entry. The Idle Detection specification defines this permission, Chrome's documentation describes it as the API's dedicated permission, and Chromium lists the descriptor name.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Sources: <a href=\"https://wicg.github.io/idle-detection/#permissions\" rel=\"nofollow\">specification</a>, <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/capabilities/web-apis/idle-detection\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chrome documentation</a>, <a href=\"https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/permissions/permission_descriptor.idl\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chromium IDL</a>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Addresses the <code class=\"notranslate\">idle-detection</code> checklist item in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2616274291\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/24831\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/24831/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/24831\">#24831</a>. Other descriptors listed in that issue are not covered, so this PR does not close it.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">AI disclosure: OpenAI Codex drafted this data update from the issue, the cited sources, and the repository's existing IdleDetector compatibility entry.</p>",
