        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25351731?u=c0ece93f0dabf1e298253953d28aa0f097ffa072&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Reran the collector tests on every Bun release from 1.0.0 to 1.4.2 and this fixes the entries that were off.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">fetch()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">Request</code> taking a <code class=\"notranslate\">ReadableStream</code> body landed in 1.1.39, <code class=\"notranslate\">WebAssembly.compileStreaming()</code> / <code class=\"notranslate\">instantiateStreaming()</code> in 1.2.20 (was 1.2.18), and the <code class=\"notranslate\">SubtleCrypto</code> encapsulate/decapsulate methods, <code class=\"notranslate\">getPublicKey()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">supports()</code> in 1.4.0.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">FormData.append()</code> filename support goes back to 1.0.0, but the collector's test uses an empty <code class=\"notranslate\">Blob</code>, which lost its name until 1.4.1. I left a note instead of using 1.4.1.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30703",
            "title": "Correct some of Bun's conformance",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-29T19:58:44.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-29T19:57:41.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "alii",
                "url": "https://github.com/alii"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83347420?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29241.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4064318473\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29241\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29241/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29241\">#29241</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Following the guidance in the issue, this adds a <code class=\"notranslate\">vertical_oriented_table_cells</code> sub-feature to <code class=\"notranslate\">css.properties.writing-mode</code>, mirroring the existing <code class=\"notranslate\">vertical_oriented_form_controls</code> sub-feature.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Data and sources:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Chrome 92</strong>: verified by testing in the issue; tracking bug referenced via <code class=\"notranslate\">impl_url</code> (<a href=\"https://crbug.com/40183612\" rel=\"nofollow\">crbug.com/40183612</a>).</li>\n<li><strong>Firefox 47</strong>: supports vertical table cells, but rendering is not always correct (see screenshot in the issue), so it is marked as <code class=\"notranslate\">partial_implementation</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Safari 17.4</strong>: marked as <code class=\"notranslate\">partial_implementation</code>. The change enabling vertical writing modes for table cells (<a href=\"https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/commit/0d695812f5b0daef531a9760903457364d2265ff\">WebKit commit 0d69581</a>) shipped in the WebKit 618.1.10 branch (Safari 17.4), but the follow-up fix was reverted in <a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=266941\" rel=\"nofollow\">bug 266941</a> and the tracking bug <a href=\"https://webkit.org/b/266928\" rel=\"nofollow\">266928</a> is still open, so support remains incomplete. The note on the entry explains that vertical writing modes were not applied to <code class=\"notranslate\">th</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">td</code> elements before Safari 17.4, as requested in the issue.</li>\n<li>All other browsers use <code class=\"notranslate\">mirror</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Questions for reviewers:</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Should Firefox's <code class=\"notranslate\">partial_implementation</code> flag start at 47, or is there a later version where rendering is correct?</li>\n<li>The issue title says \"iOS &lt; 17\", but based on the WebKit commit history, 17.4 seems to be the first version with any (partial) support — Safari iOS therefore mirrors 17.4.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Release note</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>CSS: Added <code class=\"notranslate\">vertical_oriented_table_cells</code> subfeature to <code class=\"notranslate\">writing-mode</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30702",
            "title": "Add vertically-oriented table cells sub-feature to writing-mode",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-29T22:43:21.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-29T15:57:20.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "CloaRK",
                "url": "https://github.com/CloaRK"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64103?u=428d3c27c9cd7efc648e17dfe5a4321c3f8e44d2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">pseudo()</code> method of <code class=\"notranslate\">Element</code> objects has varying support for different values. I've tried to capture this here.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The behavior here is a the consequence of a spec change, resolved in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4261800498\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13804\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13804/hovercard?comment_id=4297936996&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13804#issuecomment-4297936996\">w3c/csswg-drafts#13804 (comment)</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I didn't actually test this but I feel reasonably confident given <a href=\"https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commit/c1e61b0aebf0c03d81690332f077d14da39efe09\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commit/c1e61b0aebf0c03d81690332f077d14da39efe09</a> and <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6516055192240128\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6516055192240128</a>.</p>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5336284266\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/4306\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/4306/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/4306\">web-platform-dx/web-features#4306</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30700",
            "title": "Add subfeatures for `api.Element.pseudo` parameter values",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-29T13:25:28.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-29T13:24:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ddbeck",
                "url": "https://github.com/ddbeck"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45960703?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/c9w5uH3eSuo/m/oG9HX5UfCQAJ\" rel=\"nofollow\">This message from intent to remove sent on Sept 28:</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We landed the required code in M156. The fenced frame element and window.fence are now stubs starting in M156. We will start the experiment to remove the stubs in M157. Thanks!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6366274495053824\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chrome Status entry (updated recently)</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This Chromium commit removed Fenced Frames API:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8144621\" rel=\"nofollow\">CL 8144621</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/chromium/chromium/commit/55fa5f273aed691fbe11a449cabf1943fb284f74\">This commit on GitHub</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/fenced-frame/fenced-frame-stub.https.html\">WPT test for stubs</a> - this explains all the <code class=\"notranslate\">notes</code> I added.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is a direct follow-up to my earlier PR deprecating Fenced Frame API <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5161427314\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30242\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30242/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30242\">#30242</a><br>\nThis is relaed to Shared Storeage API PR I created <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5568937249\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30659\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30659/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30659\">#30659</a></p>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30697",
            "title": "[Google Privacy Sandbox] Chrome 156 stubs out Fenced Frame API",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-01T15:23:58.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-29T09:06:05.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "bershanskiy",
                "url": "https://github.com/bershanskiy"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF158 implemented <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WebTransport/getStats\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">WebTransport.getStats()</code></a> in  <a href=\"https://bugzil.la/2007202\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzil.la/2007202</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds <code class=\"notranslate\">return_object_property_*</code> subfeatures for the members of the returned webTransportConnectionStats/WebTransportDatagramStats, based on the Firefox, WebKit and Deno source - thanks to Claude.<br>\n<code class=\"notranslate\">bytesSentOverhead</code> is omitted since no engine returns it (Firefox: <a href=\"https://bugzil.la/2051624\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzil.la/2051624</a>). Deno and Safari don't return anything useful, but they do expose the interfaces and mosty populate them with 0.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5617211633\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45893\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45893/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45893\">mdn/content#45893</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">NOTE I am away on holiday and won't be back until late October. If you can make changes to make this PR mergable, please do, and merge it.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30695",
            "title": "Firefox 158 supports WebTransport.getStats()",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-29T01:00:48.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-29T01:00:08.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185269030?u=1fc22565ccf4566b6f734fabaa87e03d9a31cfe4&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds the missing compatibility data for the following <code class=\"notranslate\">menus.update()</code> properties:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">icons</code> — Firefox 64</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">viewTypes</code> — Firefox 64</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">visible</code> — Firefox 63</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The compatibility data was added after investigating the Firefox WebExtensions implementation and documentation, Firefox release notes, and the related Mozilla Bugzilla issues.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The Firefox version information is based on the following sources:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">menus.update.visible</code> — Firefox 63, based on Firefox 63 release information and <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1482529\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1482529</a>.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">menus.update.icons</code> — Firefox 64, based on Firefox 64 release information and <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1414566\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1414566</a>.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">menus.update.viewTypes</code> — Firefox 64, based on Firefox 64 release information and <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1416839\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1416839</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">These properties were already part of the <code class=\"notranslate\">menus.update()</code> API surface, but were not represented as individual compatibility subfeatures in BCD.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The three properties have therefore been added as separate subfeatures under <code class=\"notranslate\">webextensions.api.menus.update</code>, following the existing BCD structure for WebExtensions API parameters and properties.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For browser support values outside Firefox, the entries follow the existing BCD compatibility data and mirroring conventions. In particular, <code class=\"notranslate\">safari_ios</code> is represented as <code class=\"notranslate\">mirror</code> for <code class=\"notranslate\">icons</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">viewTypes</code> where the BCD linter confirms that the value can be automatically mirrored from Safari.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #30615.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5544845808\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30615\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30615/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30615\">#30615</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30694",
            "title": "fix(webextensions): add menus.update property compatibility data",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-28T21:25:56.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-28T21:25:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "BHUVANSH855",
                "url": "https://github.com/BHUVANSH855"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">See <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5607637148\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45871\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/45871/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45871\">mdn/content#45871</a>.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/chromium/chromium/blob/5c3db6e201646bd7d7bf5b8bd9addfe582d260c2/third_party/WebKit/Source/modules/vr/VRStageParameters.idl\">Blink</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mozilla/gecko-dev/blob/434f167559365aee232255d9583873f1fafc2c3a/dom/webidl/VRDisplay.webidl\">Gecko</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/9dc62dce6723211fdf7dc0c1308b70c4094b468c/Source/WebCore/Modules/webvr/VRStageParameters.idl\">WebKit</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://immersive-web.github.io/webvr/spec/1.1/#interface-vrstageparameters\" rel=\"nofollow\">Spec</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30686",
            "title": "Rename VRStageParameters.sizeY to sizeZ",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-28T00:41:46.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-28T00:37:25.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
                "url": "https://github.com/Josh-Cena"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Part of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5481581871\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45745\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/45745/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45745\">mdn/content#45745</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm not sure how this is supposed to be marked, but IMO it's \"partially implemented\" and not \"not implemented\"—it has IDL bindings, the IDL binding returns the right value (<code class=\"notranslate\">stretch</code> vs <code class=\"notranslate\">align</code>), etc.; the property just has no rendering effect.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30677",
            "title": "Data for svg.elements.textPath.method",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-02T18:47:58.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-25T17:39:15.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
                "url": "https://github.com/Josh-Cena"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 150 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">focusgroup</code> global attribute, the related <code class=\"notranslate\">focusgroupstart</code> global attribute, and their reflected DOM properties. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5637601087193088\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5637601087193088</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds support for the four features listed above. In particular, for the <code class=\"notranslate\">focusgroup</code> attribute, I've added an individual datapoint for each of the attribute's <a href=\"https://open-ui.org/components/scoped-focusgroup.explainer/#focusgroup-tokens\" rel=\"nofollow\">tokens</a> and <a href=\"https://open-ui.org/components/scoped-focusgroup.explainer/#supported-behaviors\" rel=\"nofollow\">behaviors</a>. I have given the behaviors a prefix so they will all be kept together in the BCD table.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Notes:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The features are currently listed as non-standard because the spec PR is still open: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3466650602\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11723\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/pull/11723/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11723\">whatwg/html#11723</a>.</li>\n<li>I am currently working on documenting only the <a href=\"https://open-ui.org/components/scoped-focusgroup.explainer/\" rel=\"nofollow\">v1 focusgroup</a> features, which are all implemented. The <a href=\"https://open-ui.org/components/focusgroup-v2.explainer/\" rel=\"nofollow\">v2 focusgroup</a> features are currently experimental and subject to change, so I will handle them in a separate project in the future.</li>\n<li>The WebIDL for the DOM properties is listed in the <a href=\"https://open-ui.org/components/scoped-focusgroup.explainer/#feature-detection\" rel=\"nofollow\">feature detection</a> section of the explainer.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">cc <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/janewman/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/janewman\">@janewman</a> for technical input/questions. If you could check these to make sure I've not missed anything, that would be much appreciated. Thanks!</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30671",
            "title": "Chrome 150 focusgroup global attribute",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-25T10:43:32.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-25T10:42:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185269030?u=1fc22565ccf4566b6f734fabaa87e03d9a31cfe4&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add a note to the Firefox compatibility data for <code class=\"notranslate\">URLPattern</code> documenting that lookahead and lookbehind assertions were not supported before Firefox 149.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">URLPattern</code> API itself remains supported from Firefox 142; this change documents the historical limitation in its regular expression support rather than changing the API's <code class=\"notranslate\">version_added</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Additional details:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1998871\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1998871</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1984171\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1984171</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Bug 1998871 documents the <code class=\"notranslate\">URLPattern</code> lookahead failure in Firefox 146 and records the fix in Firefox 149.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29092.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3969152922\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29092\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29092/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29092\">#29092</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30665",
            "title": "fix(api): document `URLPattern` regex support in Firefox",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-24T21:40:45.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-24T21:40:10.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "BHUVANSH855",
                "url": "https://github.com/BHUVANSH855"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185269030?u=1fc22565ccf4566b6f734fabaa87e03d9a31cfe4&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Mark <code class=\"notranslate\">WebTransportSendStream.getWriter()</code> as partially supported in Firefox because it returns <code class=\"notranslate\">WritableStreamDefaultWriter</code> instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">WebTransportWriter</code>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>See [<a href=\"https://bugzil.la/2008673\" rel=\"nofollow\">bug 2008673</a>](<a href=\"https://bugzil.la/2008673\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzil.la/2008673</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29152.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4006815884\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29152\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29152/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29152\">#29152</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30664",
            "title": "fix(api): mark WebTransportSendStream.getWriter as partial in Firefox",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-24T21:17:15.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-24T21:16:25.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "BHUVANSH855",
                "url": "https://github.com/BHUVANSH855"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64103?u=428d3c27c9cd7efc648e17dfe5a4321c3f8e44d2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Set partial for <code class=\"notranslate\">html.elements.img.sizes.auto</code> due to squashed SVG rendering</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324661\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324661</a> has a good description of the bug, a test case, and a screenshot comparing the results across browsers.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://checkoutworks.dev/blogs/shopify-field-notes/shopify-horizon-svg-squashed-safari-27\" rel=\"nofollow\">workaround blog post</a> also shows that widely-used Shopify theme is affected by this bug.</p>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Caught in the course of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5569192978\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/4422\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/web-platform-dx/web-features/pull/4422/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/pull/4422\">web-platform-dx/web-features#4422</a>. I kept the feature from advancing to Baseline newly available while we consider this.</li>\n</ul>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30663",
            "title": "`html.elements.img.sizes.auto`: set Safari as partial due to SVG bug",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-24T17:52:03.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-24T17:51:27.000Z",
